# ─── Tavvit Configuration ────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env and configure, or run ./install.sh to generate it for you.
# Tavvit is private by default: with this file left at its defaults nobody can
# register, nothing is shared with other servers, and nothing phones home.

# Your server's public domain name (required). A hostname, not a URL. If the
# public port is not 443, put it here (chat.example.com:1443); that only works in
# proxy mode, see below.
DOMAIN=example.com

# ─── Deployment mode ───────────────────────────────────────
# How this instance is exposed to the internet. ./install.sh sets these for you;
# only touch them for a fully manual setup.
#
#   allinone  (default) — the bundled Caddy owns ports 80/443 and does automatic
#                         HTTPS for DOMAIN. Requires 80/443 free on this host.
#   proxy               — you run your OWN reverse proxy (nginx, Traefik, Caddy,
#                         Nginx Proxy Manager, SWAG …). No bundled Caddy; the app
#                         is published on 127.0.0.1:APP_PORT for your proxy to
#                         forward to. Use with:
#                           docker compose -f docker-compose.yml \
#                             -f docker-compose.proxy.yml up -d
#   tunnel              — same as proxy, but fronted by a tunnel (Cloudflare
#                         Tunnel, Tailscale …). Point the tunnel's ingress at
#                         http://127.0.0.1:APP_PORT. NOTE: voice/WebRTC does NOT
#                         traverse a tunnel, and Cloudflare caps request bodies
#                         at 100 MB — set MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE below that (see below).
DEPLOY_MODE=allinone

# Host loopback port the app is published on in `proxy`/`tunnel` mode (ignored in
# `allinone` mode). Your reverse proxy / tunnel forwards to 127.0.0.1:APP_PORT.
# APP_PORT=8080

# How many proxies sit in front of this app and may be trusted to have written
# the X-Forwarded-For header. This is the address every rate limit counts a
# request against, so it has to match your topology:
#
#   0  nothing in front at all: the app is exposed directly on its own port.
#      The header is ignored entirely and the socket address is used. Do not leave
#      this at 1: from inside the app one proxy and one client that made the
#      header up look exactly the same, so a directly exposed instance at 1
#      believes whatever a client sends and its rate limits can be evaded.
#   1  (default) the bundled Caddy, your own reverse proxy, or a tunnel
#      daemon. Every mode above is one hop.
#   2  a CDN (Cloudflare proxied DNS, Fastly …) in FRONT of your own reverse
#      proxy, WHEN that proxy appends to X-Forwarded-For (nginx with the
#      snippet install.sh prints does). At 1 the app would see the CDN's
#      address and put everyone behind it in a single rate-limit bucket.
#      If the proxy in front of the app is the BUNDLED CADDY, this number
#      alone does nothing: Caddy throws the CDN's entry away unless its
#      trusted_proxies names the CDN, so the app gets the CDN's address at
#      any count. Configure trusted_proxies in the Caddyfile first.
#
# Your proxy config needs nothing special for this: appending to
# X-Forwarded-For (nginx's $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for) is exactly right, and so
# is Caddy's overwrite. Too low costs a shared bucket; too high hands the key
# back to the client, so when in doubt go lower. The server refuses to start,
# with a message, on any value that is not a non-negative integer and on
# anything above 4. Leaving the line blank (TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=) is not an
# error; it reads as unset and you get the default of 1.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# ─── Server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production/Docker listen port (Caddy reverse-proxies to it). Local development
# ignores this and uses 3005 — the Vite dev proxy target — set by `pnpm dev`.
PORT=3000
HOST=0.0.0.0

# ─── Authentication (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────
# Secret that signs login tokens. This MUST be set to a strong random value.
# Leaving it empty is intentional — `docker compose up` then fails immediately
# with a clear message instead of the server boot-looping. Generate one with:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
# (./install.sh fills this in for you automatically.) Must be at least 32
# characters. Keep this file private (chmod 600 .env) and never commit it:
# anyone who has the secret can mint a login token for any account. Changing it
# signs everybody out.
JWT_SECRET=

# ─── Who can join ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Registration is CLOSED. Accounts are made two ways:
#   * the administrator creates invite links (Settings → Instance → Registration):
#     expiring, limited-use, revocable; or
#   * you create an account on the server: ./tavvit-admin.sh create <name> --member
#
# The FIRST administrator is created the second way, once, after the first start:
#     ./tavvit-admin.sh create <your-name> --admin
# There is deliberately no "first visitor becomes admin" window.
#
# Set this to true only if you want anyone who finds the address to be able to
# sign up. (An administrator can also flip it later in the app; that choice wins
# over this line.)
REGISTRATION_OPEN=false

# ─── Federation (OFF) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Linking this server with other Backspace/Tavvit servers (friends and DMs across
# servers, "Connections"). Off means: the federation endpoints do not exist, no
# request is ever made to another server, and the browser may only talk to this
# server and your voice server. A server for one group of friends does not need it.
# Turning it on restores the upstream federation behaviour.
# FEDERATION_ENABLED=false

# Max file upload size in bytes (default: 100MB)
# TUNNEL USERS: Cloudflare (free/pro) hard-caps request bodies at 100 MB, so the
# 100 MB default lets uploads fail at the edge. Set this below the cap, e.g.
# 94371840 (90 MB), leaving headroom for multipart overhead. install.sh does
# this automatically when you pick `tunnel` mode.
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=104857600

# Peer origins reach this instance two ways. An admin can name one (the peering
# screen, an approved peer row), or a caller can assert one (a friend handle
# someone typed, a callback to a peering request that was never accepted).
# Asserted origins must resolve to a public address before this instance will
# send a request to them. Only matters with FEDERATION_ENABLED=true. Turn this on
# for a LAN-only deployment where every instance sits on a private address.
# FEDERATION_ALLOW_PRIVATE_PEERS=false

# ─── AGPL-3.0 § 13 source offer (YOU MUST SET THIS) ─────────
# Tavvit is a MODIFIED version of Backspace, licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0. The
# licence requires that everyone who uses a modified version over a network can
# get the source code of THAT version. An install from a release archive serves it
# itself (publish-source.sh) and needs nothing here. From a git checkout, or if you
# prefer a public repository, put its address here. The app shows a "Source code"
# link in Settings and on About. See docs/tavvit/LICENSING.md.
# TAVVIT_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/<you>/tavvit
#
# Short git commit of the running build. Baked in automatically by install.sh and
# update.sh at image build time; leave unset for local development.
# BACKSPACE_COMMIT=

# ─── Image ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image is built from this checkout and tagged tavvit:local. Compose never
# pulls it (there is no public Tavvit image; the one upstream publishes is
# Backspace). To run an image you publish yourself, uncomment all three and install
# with BACKSPACE_BUILD=false.
# BACKSPACE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/<you>/tavvit
# BACKSPACE_IMAGE_TAG=latest
# BACKSPACE_PULL_POLICY=missing

# ─── LiveKit Voice/Video ───────────────────────────────────
# To enable voice/video, fill in all three values below and add:
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=voice
# Leave empty to run Tavvit without voice features. The same key and secret must be
# in livekit.yaml (./install.sh writes both). Voice needs UDP ports open on the
# server: 3478/udp, 7881/tcp and 50000-60000/udp. See docs/tavvit/VOICE.md.
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
# Where the server itself reaches LiveKit, to put someone out of a call. docker-compose.yml sets this.
# LIVEKIT_API_URL=http://host.docker.internal:7880

# ─── Desktop App (Electron) ───────────────────────────────
# Override the URL that the desktop app loads (auto-detects in dev/prod)
# BACKSPACE_URL=https://my-instance.com

# Auto-update server URL for electron-updater (optional)
# BACKSPACE_UPDATE_URL=https://releases.example.com

# ─── Docker Compose ────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment to enable the LiveKit service:
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=voice

# ─── Database Backups ──────────────────────────────────────
# Automatic SQLite snapshots: pre-migration (always, when a migration is pending),
# scheduled (every BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS), and manual (./backup.sh). Rotated per type.
# Snapshots cover the DATABASE only; uploaded files live in data/uploads and need
# their own backup (docs/tavvit/BACKUP-AND-RESTORE.md). Snapshots live on the same
# disk as the database: copy them off the machine.
# BACKUP_DIR=./data/backups            # default: <data>/backups
# BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=24
# BACKUP_KEEP_SCHEDULED=7
# BACKUP_KEEP_PREMIGRATION=5
# BACKUP_KEEP_MANUAL=10
# BACKUP_KEEP_CONSOLE=5                # "Back up now" in the admin console
# BACKUP_MAX_AGE_DAYS=90               # copies made by hand (manual, console) are gone after this
# Hook run INSIDE the container after each snapshot, with the snapshot path appended as the
# last argument. The image has no rclone or rsync, so use it to copy to a volume you mount
# into the container, e.g. `cp -t /offsite` (docs/tavvit/BACKUP-AND-RESTORE.md).
# BACKUP_OFFSITE_CMD=
# BACKUP_DISABLED=false
# The administrators are told when the disk is this full (and when a backup fails or is overdue).
# OPERATOR_ALERT_DISK_PERCENT=85

# ─── Two-factor authentication ──────────────────────────────
# What the secrets are encrypted with: 32 bytes. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Unset, nobody can turn 2FA on. Keep it with your backups: without it, everyone who has
# 2FA is locked out until ./tavvit-admin.sh reset-2fa <username>. Changing it has the same effect.
# TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ─── Translating messages ──
# Off by default: the browser's own translator still works where there is one (Chrome and
# Edge on a computer), and everyone else gets a link to Google Translate. With a provider,
# the words of a message go to it when someone asks. docs/systems/translation.md
# none, deepl or libretranslate:
# TRANSLATION_PROVIDER=none
# DEEPL_API_KEY=
# For LibreTranslate on this server, add translate to COMPOSE_PROFILES (voice,translate with voice) too:
# LIBRETRANSLATE_URL=http://libretranslate:5000
# LIBRETRANSLATE_API_KEY=

# ─── Email ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default. Then accounts have no address, and a forgotten password can only be
# reset by an administrator. docs/systems/email.md has the DNS records and the steps.
# none, resend or smtp:
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT=none
# EMAIL_FROM="Tavvit <no-reply@example.com>"
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
# Where links in mail lead. Default: PUBLIC_ORIGIN, then https://DOMAIN.
# APP_BASE_URL=
# For resend: a sending-only key, restricted to your domain. Keep this file at chmod 600.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Without this, the server does not hear about bounces.
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# For smtp. With a user, TLS is required.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# What the budget counts against. Default 100 and 3000 with resend (its free plan), none with smtp.
# EMAIL_DAILY_LIMIT=
# EMAIL_MONTHLY_LIMIT=

# ─── Things Tavvit does NOT do by default ───────────────────
# Tavvit sends no usage data to anyone and looks up no releases anywhere; neither
# feature exists. The outbound features are off unless you set them, the mail above
# and this:
#
# Public space directory hub. Empty = no listing, no browsing, no requests.
# DIRECTORY_ENDPOINT=
#
# Where the desktop installers are read from (served at /downloads/desktop/).
# Default: downloads/ beside the database, i.e. data/downloads (docs/systems/desktop.md, "Releases").
# DOWNLOADS_DIR=
#
# Where people's copies of their own data are kept for a week. Never under DOWNLOADS_DIR,
# which anyone can read. Default: exports/ beside the database (docs/systems/legal.md, "Data export").
# EXPORT_DIR=
#
# How this instance gets its image: prebuilt | source. install.sh writes this;
# ./update.sh reads it. Tavvit is a source install by default.
# BACKSPACE_INSTALL_CHANNEL=source
